# Copy to .env and edit. Everything in scripts/ sources scripts/env.sh, which loads that
# file, so nothing here needs exporting by hand.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# Rules, because this is parsed rather than sourced:
#   * KEY=value, one per line. `export KEY=value` is accepted too.
#   * Comments go on their own line. A '#' after a value is part of the value -- tokens
#     are allowed to contain one.
#   * Trailing whitespace on a bare value is stripped; a trailing space in a token is
#     otherwise a 1008 you will spend an evening on. Quote the value to keep it exactly.
#   * A variable already set in your shell wins, so a one-off override still works:
#       AGENT_WS_URL=wss://other ./scripts/local_client.sh
#
# Commented-out lines below are the defaults -- uncomment only to change them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the agent socket
# The Cloudflare tunnel in front of the interaction model, and the token it checks.
# A quick tunnel gets a new hostname every restart, so this is the line you will edit
# most. See docs/local-client.md.
AGENT_WS_URL=wss://REPLACE-WITH-TUNNEL-HOST.trycloudflare.com
AGENT_TOKEN=REPLACE-WITH-TOKEN

# Seconds between partial transcripts. Not phrase length -- Moonshine decides where a
# phrase ends from the audio.
#AGENT_UPDATE_INTERVAL=0.3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the game view
# The client also forwards the frame ROCKET-2 is publishing, so the model can resolve
# "mine *that*" against something. The two are separate processes on this laptop and meet
# at a file; both sides must agree on the path. Nothing is sent when no agent is running,
# so this costs nothing to leave on. See docs/local-client.md.
#AGENT_FRAMES=1
#AGENT_FRAME_INTERVAL=3.0
#MCAGENTS_FRAME_PATH=/tmp/mcagents-frame.jpg

# The agent side: seconds between publishes, 0 to publish nothing. Deliberately shorter
# than AGENT_FRAME_INTERVAL -- the two poll independently, so matching them would make the
# frame the client picks up as much as two intervals old.
#MCAGENTS_FRAME_INTERVAL=1.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- goals coming back
# The second tunnel: the JSON ROCKET-2 runs, as plan entries. Leave it unset and the model
# can still talk back over AGENT_WS_URL -- it just cannot drive the agent. Goals queue at
# MCAGENTS_GOAL_DIR for `rocket2.sh --listen`, so both processes must agree on it.
#AGENT_GOAL_WS_URL=wss://REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-GOAL-TUNNEL.trycloudflare.com
#MCAGENTS_GOAL_DIR=/tmp/mcagents-goals

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- speech recognition
# TINY_STREAMING (34M, faster, 12% WER) | SMALL_STREAMING | MEDIUM_STREAMING (245M).
#VOICE_ARCH=SMALL_STREAMING
#VOICE_LANGUAGE=en

# Input device index or name substring. Left unset, PipeWire's default source is used and
# the choice is printed at startup. `./scripts/local_client.sh --list-devices` measures
# them: on this laptop the live mic is hw:1,6, and hw:1,0 is the empty headset jack.
#VOICE_DEVICE=8

# 1 lets PortAudio's ALSA complaints through. They are noisy and harmless.
#VOICE_AUDIO_LOG=0

# The chat server for `python -m mcagents.voice` -- deliberately separate from
# JARVISVLA_URL, because sharing one vLLM with a once-per-step policy makes rollouts
# stutter whenever anyone speaks. See docs/voice.md.
#VOICE_LLM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
#VOICE_MAX_TOKENS=200

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the GPU box
# Read by scripts/connect.sh. NODE_IP changes every Slurm allocation -- take the first
# 172.20.x address from `hostname -I` on the compute node, not the short hostname, which
# the login node cannot resolve. serve_jarvisvla.sh prints the command.
#USER_HOST=szeng26@ssh.ccv.brown.edu
#NODE_IP=172.20.237.6
#PORT=8000
# 0 disables ssh -C, which is the right call on a fast link.
#COMPRESS=1

# The JarvisVLA policy, through that tunnel.
#JARVISVLA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- this machine
# /tmp is emptied at boot, which wipes the downloaded simulator engine.
#MINESTUDIO_DIR=$HOME/.minestudio
#DISPLAY=:1

# Attach to an already-running Minecraft instead of booting one (scripts/mc_server.sh).
#MC_PORT=9000
